The IDE no longer reports a member as verified, or as finished, before every check at the member's position has been prepared, when a refining module checks again the override of a class member it inherits (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/433). Since https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/404, that check belongs to a copy of the member, at the member's own position. The position's preparation state was one value for the member and its copy, and became done as soon as either one's tasks were identified. So if the copy's check finished first, the member read as verified until its own tasks were identified, even when one of them then failed, and a counterexample request could return without the member's counterexamples. The position now stays in preparation while any check scheduled at it is still being prepared.
